			<abstract>
				<p>Sentiment bias is newly discovered in Recommender Systems (RSs). Critical users and niche items are disadvantaged by such unfair recommendations. To mitigate this bias, we propose a novel approach by counterfactual inference, which is implemented in two stages. Experiment results validate that our model achieves comparable performance in rating prediction, providing better recommendations and effectively mitigating sentiment bias. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first work to employ counterfactual inference on sentiment bias mitigation in RSs. CCS Concepts • Computing methodologies → Causal reasoning and diagnostics.</p>
			</abstract>
